  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: PreS&E 1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: 'A research team is planning a large preclinical research project that
    will require funding, lab space, and shared resources across several departments.


    <b>The
    study sponsor may review the project to ensure it is feasible, properly resourced,
    and aligned with research policies before it moves forward.</b>


    Is this
    <b>true</b> or <b>false</b>?'
  explanation: Sponsors help confirm that a study has the funding, staff, space,
    and systems needed to be carried out responsibly. They also check that the project
    follows organizational policies and ethical standards. This helps ensure the
    research can be completed as planned and managed safely from start to finish.
  correctAnswer: True
  incorrectAnswer1: False
  incorrectAnswer2: 
  incorrectAnswer3: 
  questionRole: Safety & Ethics
  questionType: TrueFalse
  questionStage: PreClinical
